## Overall Thoughts
Clankvasion was a fun project that let us combine tower defense with active shooting. I focused mainly on the user interface and tower placement systems.

## Sprint-by-Sprint Reflection

### Sprint 1
- **What I worked on:** Basic UI layout and currency display.
- **Difficulties:** Getting the HUD to stay clean while showing important information.
- **Lessons Learned:** UI should be functional before it looks good.

### Sprint 2
- **What I worked on:** Tower shop menu and upgrade menu for the Main Tower.
- **Difficulties:** Making the menus easy to use without interfering with mouse aiming.
- **Surprises:** The upgrade menu for the Main Tower became one of the most polished parts.

### Sprint 3
- **What I worked on:** Tower placement system (free placement on map) and visual feedback.
- **Difficulties:** Preventing towers from being placed on top of each other or in invalid spots.
- **Lessons Learned:** Good visual feedback (green/red placement indicators) is extremely important.

### Sprint 4
- **What I worked on:** Pause menu, settings, win/lose screens, and overall UI polish.
- **Difficulties:** Making the pause menu look nice with the transparent overlay.
- **Lessons Learned:** Polish and small details take more time than expected but are worth it.

## Major Challenges
- Designing UI that doesn’t block the player’s view during intense shooting moments.
- Coordinating with Bryce on the upgrade systems.

## Key Lessons Learned
- User experience matters as much as gameplay.
- Keeping UI code clean and modular helps when changes are requested.
- Playtesting with fresh eyes helps catch confusing UI elements.

## What I Contributed
- All menus (shop, upgrades, pause)
- Tower purchasing and placement system
- Currency UI and feedback
- Win/Lose screens and game flow

## Final Thoughts
I really enjoyed working on the UX side of the game. Seeing players easily understand and enjoy the menus and placement system was very satisfying. This project taught me a lot about Godot UI tools and the importance of good user feedback.

